{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And he dressed him in garments of fine linen.</b> Rashi explained: it is a thing of importance in Egypt. And some challenge this from what he explained in the chapter Bereshit regarding the river Pishon — that it is the Nile, and it is called Pishon because it grows flax — which implies that flax was common in Egypt. And it seems to me: certainly it grows flax, and it is more important than all lands, and because of its importance it was expensive, and this is what Rashi of blessed memory said: it is of importance in Egypt. And further, one may say that the flax mentioned there is hemp, as in ״ותטמנם בפשתי העץ״ which Rashi explained as hemp, while the שש here is linen, and it was not common in Egypt."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:55.785886416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}